  {
   "title": "Blue Notes, Heavy Debts",
   "logline": "A jazz guitarist who bets everything on a jazz-metal hybrid watches his ambitions, friendships, and finances collapse until he is left with nothing but his instruments' ghosts.",
   "sentences": [
    {
     "index": 2,
     "text": "The hybrid demo hit the clubs like lightning, and Mike's new label offered him a fat advance, though the band he once led quietly stopped returning his calls."
    },
    {
     "index": 3,
     "text": "Mike signed a studio lease and bought a rack of gleaming amps, but his old drummer refused to play the fusion set and openly mocked his new direction."
    },
    {
     "index": 4,
     "text": "Mike's hybrid album topped the indie charts, his bank account swelled with royalties, and he finally made peace with the bandmates who had doubted him."
    },
    {
     "index": 5,
     "text": "Mike booked a sold-out tour across three countries, and his new bassist and vocalist welcomed him as a true brother after the late-night rehearsals."
    },
    {
     "index": 6,
     "text": "A venue owner skipped the payment, the label froze his royalties, and Mike pawned his vintage Gibson while the band whispered that he had gone too far."
    },
    {
     "index": 7,
     "text": "Mike woke in a cold storage unit, his last amp seized for debt, clutching the only bandmate still beside him and swearing the hybrid sound would survive."
    }
   ],
