  {
   "title": "The Hybrid Sound Ledger",
   "logline": "A broke jazz guitarist who dreams of fusing jazz with heavy metal rebuilds his band and his belief in the hybrid sound after losing nearly everything.",
   "sentences": [
    {
     "index": 2,
     "text": "After the club folded, Mike pawned his Gibson and sold his amplifier, then watched the bandmates walk away without a word."
    },
    {
     "index": 3,
     "text": "One night a former bassist returned with a borrowed amp, quietly asking whether Mike still remembered the lost metal riffs."
    },
    {
     "index": 4,
     "text": "At a cramped rehearsal, the bandmates trusted Mike to lead the riffs, though his rent was overdue and his guitar sat in hock."
    },
    {
     "index": 5,
     "text": "Hearing a distorted tritone bend into a swinging ride cymbal, Mike felt certain the hybrid sound was finally breathing on its own."
    },
    {
     "index": 6,
     "text": "Convinced the fusion would carry them, Mike sketched a set list, though the landlord still threatened eviction over unpaid rent."
    },
    {
     "index": 7,
     "text": "By week's end, Mike was certain the hybrid sound would change everything, though the eviction notice waited taped to his door."
    }
   ],
