  {
   "title": "Blood Money Blues",
   "logline": "A broke jazz guitarist chasing a jazz-metal fusion sound gets pulled into a loan shark's debt, and the price of his survival is his loyal band.",
   "sentences": [
    {
     "index": 2,
     "text": "At the Blue Lantern, Mike's jazz-metal set lifted the crowd, though his rent was three months overdue."
    },
    {
     "index": 3,
     "text": "A jaded critic called the fusion a gimmick, and Mike, shaken, started doubting the whole experiment."
    },
    {
     "index": 4,
     "text": "After a pawnbroker seized his amplifier, Mike doubled down on the hybrid sound, convinced one brutal rehearsal would save it."
    },
    {
     "index": 5,
     "text": "A loan shark's collector tailed Mike home, but his drummer and bassist pledged their savings to cover the debt."
    },
    {
     "index": 6,
     "text": "In a rain-soaked alley, Mike's bandmates stood beside him when the collector's men broke two of his fingers."
    },
    {
     "index": 7,
     "text": "Days later, Mike took the club owner's blood money, a steady residency, and his bandmates vanished, refusing every call."
    }
   ],
