  {
   "title": "Applause Without Accompaniment",
   "logline": "A jazz guitarist chasing a jazz-metal fusion triumph wins fame and prestige while his bandmates drift away and his finances collapse.",
   "sentences": [
    {
     "index": 2,
     "text": "Mike won a prestigious commission for a jazz-metal suite, though his bandmates quietly stopped returning his calls."
    },
    {
     "index": 3,
     "text": "Mike's gala premiere sold out in minutes, yet at rehearsal the drummer greeted him with a pointed, theatrical silence."
    },
    {
     "index": 4,
     "text": "A critic praised the crowd's ecstatic applause but called the fusion a charming, well-dressed argument with itself."
    },
    {
     "index": 5,
     "text": "At the victory reception Mike was toasted by strangers, while the chairs reserved for his bandmates stayed pointedly empty."
    },
    {
     "index": 6,
     "text": "Mike's glowing festival invitation arrived the same week his promoter admitted the commission would pay only in exposure."
    },
    {
     "index": 7,
     "text": "Mike pawned his vintage Gibson to cover the festival's travel costs, then headlined to a standing ovation, alone."
    }
   ],
