  {
   "title": "The Hybrid Sound Burns",
   "logline": "A broke jazz guitarist chases a heavy-metal fusion that his devoted bandmates believe in, then abandons it at the height of his success before returning to it on his own terms.",
   "sentences": [
    {
     "index": 2,
     "text": "Mike pawned his amplifier that week, convinced the metal experiment was a dead end, yet his bandmates cheered his solo anyway."
    },
    {
     "index": 3,
     "text": "Mike sold a studio session and felt the fusion sound finally click, as the quartet hailed his tangled, heavy-jazz riffs."
    },
    {
     "index": 4,
     "text": "Mike signed a steady teaching post and recorded the hybrid album, with bandmates insisting he lead the next tour."
    },
    {
     "index": 5,
     "text": "Mike began doubting the hybrid sound after a critic called the record clumsy, though the festival still booked his quartet headlining."
    },
    {
     "index": 6,
     "text": "Mike burned every metal sketch in the studio trash barrel, swearing the fusion experiment was dead forever, while the festival crowd roared for pure jazz."
    },
    {
     "index": 7,
     "text": "Mike returned to the sketches months later, rewriting riffs with joy, while a grant letter arrived and his bandmates agreed to try again."
    }
   ],
